Native metric adapters used by codec_vis

All production adapters consume planar FP32 linear BT.2020 D65 (FP16 working
space semantics widened to FP32), 1.0 = 203 cd/m². No metric subprocesses,
Python, CUDA, integer images, display RGB conversions, or gamut reduction.
FP64 accumulation is used where appropriate. CPU implementations are linked
normally into the executable. Their original license notices are retained.

Butteraugli
  Source: https://github.com/google/butteraugli
  Files obtained 2026-10-16 from the standalone upstream master branch.
  Apache-2.0, Google Inc. This is the standalone Google model, not libjxl's
  different Butteraugli revision. The API's floating-point 255 unit scale
  does not imply 8-bit quantization.
  Changes: original photopsin matrix composed with BT.2020 -> XYZ -> BT.709;
  no intermediate BT.709 RGB image. The calibrated rational response is
  unchanged within its specified domain, with a continuous tangent extension
  outside that domain. Edge replication handles images smaller than 8x8.
  SDR parity tests compare unmodified upstream reference scores: error <=1e-4.
  Unmodified source SHA-256:
    butteraugli.cc a5f0ae1696955e33a2761395ef6df4ffa320812626324161bb8215d2d9b47c58
    butteraugli.h  64d0c2838a307ef603cfe376976df4f2c246898c021dde5468cf63bcd1737231

ColorVideoVDP
  Source: fcvvdp v0.4.0, Halide Compression, LLC; copyright and license
  notices are retained in third_party/fcvvdp.
  Apache-2.0. Includes that project's planar-float API.
  Changes: compose original RGB->XYZ matrix for direct BT.2020; remove the
  SDR/HDR RGB clamp in display application. Only the audited scalar kernels
  are dispatched. Planar FP32 input is passed directly; the upstream library
  copies it into its mutable workspace. No byte/integer input API is used.
  Display: standard 30-inch 4K, 200-nit SDR model. HDR is evaluated as an
  unclipped extension; scores are not claimed calibrated for HDR.
  SDR reference fixtures agree within 1e-5 JOD.
  Unmodified cvvdp.c SHA-256:
    2a2bcf8c4be2d9ab529d7dedb5bf89f3a3103e97cf1870581195aac98d16f2fb

The previous PSNR-HVS/libvmaf adapter is removed: it accepted integer YUV
pictures, not the required linear floating-point working space. No replacement
is offered under that name.

Admission policy
  gui/metrics.cpp::metric_catalog is the sole offered list. Each admitted
  descriptor has a typed linear-BT.2020 evaluator, direction, units and a
  calibration note. Add adapters there only with SDR reference parity,
  identity, HDR/wide-gamut/negative-value and sub-8-bit precision tests.
  Reject or remove entries whose implementations clamp to an RGB gamut,
  quantize image samples to integers, spawn processes, or use non-Vulkan GPU
  APIs. Approximate HDR calibration is disclosed while scores are produced.
  Lazy worker and UI consume the registry and need no metric-specific cases.
